g a  drug-addicted boxer bale not only  dropped 70 pounds for the roll he  elected to have a custom mouth of broken  and decaying teeth glued down over his  regular teeth for the duration of  shooting  number 13  another thing that we'll probably hear a  lot on this video is the name gary  archer a dental lab technician by trade  archer has made a career out of building  custom prosthetics and veneers for some  of the biggest names in hollywood and  how did he get his start well maybe you  remember a little movie called mrs  doubtfire archer and actor robin  williams worked together to build a  custom set of loose-fitting dentures  that could drop out of william's mouth  for that iconic drinking gag  i'll be right back  i just have to reattach some little heat  number 12.  in 1994 jim carrey played the lead in a  whopping three films but we're not here  to chat about the mask or aceventure a  pet detective even if carrie wore those  gigantic dentures for the mask instead  let's take a look at dumb and dumber to  get ready for the roll carrie had a  previous bit of dental surgery reversed  removing a cap from one of his front  teeth to create lloyd's wild chipped up  grin  oh yeah  number eleven  shia labeouf has a reputation these days  as a guy who will do just about anything  for a role most of the time that means  putting on or losing some weight staying  locked up inside to lose a fan or  messing with your sleep schedule to  become nocturnal for a while  on fury la buff went a lot further to  create the illusion of being a soldier  who has gone through the horrors of  world war ii the actor had both of his  front teeth pulled  creating a huge gap in his smile that  had to be filled again after shooting  number 10  one of the most famous examples on this  list has to be johnny depp in the  pirates of the caribbean franchise to  help create the grimy scummy look of  captain jack sparrow depp opted to have  several of his teeth capped over with  gold during shooting giving himself the  look of a lifelong pirate whose  hard-living and constant rum drinking  has left him with a ruined set of pearly  yellows  number nine  singer-songwriter freddie mercury was  known for always going big as the front  man of queen big performances big energy  and well big teeth the performer  suffered from several additional teeth  at the back of his mouth which pushed  his normal teeth forward into a  substantial and instantly recognizable  overbite actor rami malik had to  recreate this effect for the film  bohemian rhapsody slotting in sizable  dentures and having to learn how to talk  and sing around his mouth being forced  into a new and uncomfortable shape  number eight  let's get old school for a minute and  talk about the horror classic the  haunted strangler as boris karloff's  character becomes increasingly possessed  by the ghost of a serial murderer he  takes on an increasingly grotesque and  corpse-like appearance to create this  look karloff removed his false teeth and  sucked in his cheeks to give his face a  sunken appearance  and his lips were partially wired shut  to give him a constant sneer  number seven  for her oscar-winning portrayal of  serial killer eileen wuornos in monster  charlize theron spent multiple hours  every day in the makeup chair to have  prosthetics and makeup applied to give  her a haggard and weather-worn  appearance  it's a remarkable transformation for the  south african actress especially at only  28 years old and is only aided by the  addition of a set of nasty rotted out  prosthetic teeth that had to be tacked  down into the actress's mouth every day  number six  robert de niro went all out to prepare  for the role of max katie in cape fear  stripping himself back to only four  percent body fat and having multiple  tattoos done in vegetable dyes that  would fade after shooting  he also and this one is kind of creepy  paid a dentist thousands of dollars to  have the guy go to town on his teeth  grindin